                        "glosses": [
                            "The amount that a breast will carry or hold."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6276205c-1552-4af1-9d4d-1a8f317a1137",
                                "sense_id": "138e8d5f-621f-3818-9d42-aa27aafefa0f",
                                "text": "Enough for Him whom cherubim Worship night and day, A breastful of milk And a mangerful of hay; Enough for Him whom angels Fall down before, The ox and ass and camel Which adore."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "986097b8-916e-473f-aa5f-266515f8fffd",
                                "sense_id": "138e8d5f-621f-3818-9d42-aa27aafefa0f",
                                "text": "And again he inhaled a prodigious breastful of the mountain air. \""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d102f1a2-7a20-4fb6-a24a-8faccff644a5",
                                "sense_id": "138e8d5f-621f-3818-9d42-aa27aafefa0f",
                                "text": "I had expected him to be a middle-aged man with a breastful of medals, with whom I would have to be formal; but Dunn was actually two months younger than myself."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a4eb9002-bebf-4b64-ab5b-668ab873cdb3",
                                "sense_id": "138e8d5f-621f-3818-9d42-aa27aafefa0f",
                                "text": "There were conjurers and singers and highland dancers wearing breastsful of medals, funny stories and recitations by blushing boys, and finally the choir again."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
